Continuwuity on FenrirOS
========================

Installed inert: the service is not enabled and there is no configuration,
server name, signing key or registration token.

    cp /usr/share/doc/continuwuity/conduwuit-example.toml /etc/continuwuity/continuwuity.toml
    chgrp continuwuity /etc/continuwuity/continuwuity.toml; chmod 640 /etc/continuwuity/continuwuity.toml
    $EDITOR /etc/continuwuity/continuwuity.toml
    # set server_name (permanent! it is part of every user id and cannot be changed later),
    # [global] address/port, database_path = "/var/lib/continuwuity/db",
    # allow_registration with a registration_token (or leave registration off), allow_federation
    dinitctl enable continuwuity

Federation needs the server name to resolve to the server: serve
/.well-known/matrix/server and /.well-known/matrix/client from your web server
or open port 8448 with a certificate; a reverse proxy (nginx, caddy) with TLS in
front of port 6167 is the usual setup. The first user to register on a fresh
server becomes its admin; the server also takes admin commands in the admin
room it creates. Voice/video calls: the coturn package (turn_uris, turn_secret).
The binary is conduwuit (continuwuity is a link to it).
